From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ronny=20Kr=C3=BCger?=
 <197308427+dangelrk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 10:49:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Make the ace compiler buildable as a host cross-compiler

ace is a pure text-in/text-out translator: it reads BASIC with stdio,
writes 68000 assembly with fprintf, and resolves library functions from
the .bmap files on disk rather than from the running system.  The whole
AmigaOS surface was 11 call sites in 5 files, so it ports cleanly.

  hostcompat.h  exact-width Amiga base types for ACE_HOST builds.  LONG
                must stay 32 bits (FLOAT_BITS) and SHORT 16 bits (.bmap
                LVOs rely on the wraparound for negative offsets).
  alloc.c       AllocRemember/FreeRemember -> a malloc chain.  Same
                semantics, no intuition.library, builds on both sides.
  break.c       new: Ctrl-C handling behind install_break_handler() and
                break_requested().  Separate module because acedef.h
                declares ACE's own kill(), which collides with POSIX
                kill() from <signal.h>.
  lex.c         dropped open/close_shared_libs(): the intuition.library
                base it fetched was never dereferenced.
  libfunc.c     .bmap reading via fopen/fread; ACE_BMAPS overrides the
                ACEbmaps: assign (falls back to it when unset).
  parse.c       ACE_HOME overrides ACE:icons/exe.info likewise.

Also fixes three latent defects that the port made reachable:

  assign.c      fsize() never checked fopen(), so a missing .bmap
                segfaulted in fseek() instead of raising error 50.  It
                also returned unsigned, making the caller's == -1L test
                dead.  Now returns long/-1.
  codegen.c     with the crash above gone, a failed DECLARE left libname
                NULL and the eventual call crashed in strcmp().  Guard it.
  parse.c       the icon copy loop used feof(), appending one stray 0xFF
                byte to every generated .info file.

14 %ld/%lx conversions took LONG arguments, which is fine where int and
long are both 32 bits but corrupts emitted constants on LP64 hosts.
FLOAT_BITS.l is now ULONG so negative float literals can't sign-extend.
Makefile-host keeps -Werror=format so this cannot regress.

Verified on macOS arm64: 223 of verify/tests/cases compile with no
errors and no crashes, the 28 errors/ cases are all still rejected,
1.5 emits #$3fc00000 and DATA -1.5 emits bfc00000 (IEEE 754), and
DisplayBeep resolves through the .bmap to jsr -96(a6).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
